# RONI — environment variables
#
# M1 does not use any of these yet. The app runs entirely on local,
# in-memory sample data. This file exists so the shape of future
# configuration is documented in the repo without ever committing a
# real value. Copy this file to `.env.local` (already git-ignored) and
# fill it in only when a later milestone actually wires the service up.

# --- Supabase (M3.0 — infrastructure only, no UI wired up yet) ---
# Both are safe to expose to the browser: NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is
# just your project's URL, and the publishable key (Supabase's newer
# replacement for the old "anon key") carries no special privilege —
# Row Level Security decides what it can actually read or write. Never
# put a Supabase *secret* key (sb_secret_..., formerly "service_role")
# in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable — M3.0 doesn't use one at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- AI policy extraction (M3.3 — real, wired up; optional) ---
# Server-only, never exposed to the client (only read in
# src/lib/services/policy-extraction/anthropic-provider.ts, which runs
# server-side). The Anthropic provider is now the DEFAULT extraction
# provider (real, multimodal understanding of the actual policy PDF —
# not just flattened text) — with this unset, uploads are recorded and
# stored exactly as before, but extraction honestly reports
# "needs_review" instead of guessing anything, the same safe behavior
# as every other missing-config case in this app. Set this to turn on
# real AI policy understanding.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Which PolicyExtractionProvider the Wallet uses
# (src/lib/services/policy-extraction/index.ts). Leave unset for the
# default: the real, multimodal Anthropic provider above (requires
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). Set to "text-extract" to use the older, non-AI
# PDF-text + regex/keyword extractor instead (no AI call, more limited
# understanding of tables/columns). Set to "dev-fallback" to force the
# always-empty development fallback.
# POLICY_EXTRACTION_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Which Claude model the Anthropic extraction provider calls. Optional —
# defaults to claude-sonnet-5 if unset.
# ANTHROPIC_EXTRACTION_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# Which Claude model powers Ask Roni's real PDF-grounded responses. Optional —
# defaults to claude-sonnet-5-5 (or ANTHROPIC_EXTRACTION_MODEL when set).
# ANTHROPIC_ASK_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY: set this to "dev-fallback" to exercise the old
# deterministic test adapter. Leave unset in production: when Anthropic is not
# configured, Ask Roni reports that honestly rather than presenting keyword
# matching as AI.
# POLICY_QA_PROVIDER=

# --- Durable analysis job worker (RONI Bloque 1 — corrección, fix #2) ---
# REQUIRED for analysis to ever actually run once a document is
# uploaded — see supabase/migrations/0006_policy_analysis_jobs.sql,
# src/lib/services/policy-extraction/job-runner.ts, and
# src/app/api/cron/process-analysis-jobs/route.ts.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — from your Supabase project's API settings
# (the "service_role"/secret key, NOT the publishable key above). Used
# in EXACTLY ONE file (src/lib/supabase/service-role.ts), by the cron
# worker only, because a scheduled job has no user session for RLS to
# scope by. NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never expose it to
# the client — it bypasses Row Level Security entirely.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# GITHUB ACTIONS OIDC (preferred) — the committed scheduled workflow obtains
# a short-lived GitHub-signed OIDC token and the Vercel route verifies its
# signature, audience, repository, and exact workflow ref. No shared static
# secret is required between GitHub and Vercel, so the previous 401 caused by
# two different effective CRON_SECRET values cannot recur on this path.
# These values are public configuration, not secrets; the defaults below are
# already safe for demontelau-pixel/Roni-app and normally need no entry.
# GITHUB_ACTIONS_OIDC_AUDIENCE=roni-analysis-worker
# GITHUB_ACTIONS_OIDC_REPOSITORY=demontelau-pixel/Roni-app
# GITHUB_ACTIONS_OIDC_WORKFLOW_REF=demontelau-pixel/Roni-app/.github/workflows/process-analysis-jobs.yml@refs/heads/main
#
# CRON_SECRET — OPTIONAL legacy support only for a manual or third-party
# scheduler. It is no longer needed by the GitHub Actions workflow. If used,
# it must be set only in the Vercel environment and sent as
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` by that external scheduler.
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# SCHEDULING — root `vercel.json` intentionally declares NO `crons`
# entry, so this works on Vercel's Hobby (free) plan: Hobby only runs
# Vercel's own Cron feature once every 24 hours, which is too slow for
# a real upload-and-analyze flow, and a more frequent schedule there
# requires a Vercel Pro plan. Instead, point an EXTERNAL scheduler at
# the same endpoint, on whatever interval you want (every 1–5 minutes
# is reasonable) — this is the primary, supported way to run analysis
# jobs on Hobby, not a workaround:
#
#   POST https://<your-app>/api/cron/process-analysis-jobs
#   Header: GitHub OIDC bearer token (the committed GitHub workflow does this)
#   or Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET> for a legacy external scheduler.
#
# Three ways to send that request on a schedule:
#
#   1. cron-job.org (or any free HTTP-ping cron service): create a job
#      that does an HTTP POST to the URL above with the Authorization
#      header set. No code to host — just the scheduler's own UI.
#
#   2. GitHub Actions scheduled workflow — already committed at
#      `.github/workflows/process-analysis-jobs.yml`. It uses GitHub OIDC,
#      so it needs only the non-sensitive RONI_APP_URL repository secret;
#      GitHub Actions' own schedule granularity is 5 minutes minimum.
#
#   3. Upstash QStash's own scheduling feature, pointed at the same URL
#      with the same header — a good option if you'd rather not rely
#      on GitHub Actions or a third-party free-tier cron pinger staying
#      available.
#
# If you later upgrade to Vercel Pro and want Vercel's native Cron
# instead, add a `crons` array back to `vercel.json` (Vercel sends the
# same `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` header automatically when
# you set `CRON_SECRET` as a project environment variable) — the route
# itself needs no change either way.

# --- Insurance data partners (planned, not yet integrated) ---
# BINDABLE_API_KEY=
# BINDABLE_REF_CODE=

# --- CMS Marketplace API (Health, M2.5) ---
# Server-only. Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — it must never
# reach the browser. See src/lib/services/cms/client.ts.
CMS_MARKETPLACE_API_KEY=
